config KEYLAB_LAYER_SIGNAL
    bool "Report the active layer to the host as a spare key tap"
    default y
    # Only the central owns the HID endpoints. On a peripheral the report would have nowhere to go,
    # and the peripheral's own layer state is a shadow of the central's in any case.
    depends on !ZMK_SPLIT || ZMK_SPLIT_ROLE_CENTRAL
    help
      Taps one spare key whenever the highest active layer changes, so the host can tell a
      layer-shifted key from its base-layer twin — both emit the same keycode, which is why
      everything typed from a layer is otherwise recorded as position-unattributed.

      The layer-to-key table is generated by `pnpm build` into out/layer-signal.h from
      config/layout.json5, and published in out/keymap-meta.json for the daemon that reads it.
      Set layerSignal.enabled to false there to emit nothing.
